    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text_gHCUtX2NZsXReNRd",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<h3>What if it doesn&apos;t work for me?</h3>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text_tMpAtqCuWBiR65Ui",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<h3>Here&apos;s the deal:<strong> You need to give it 30 full days</strong>. Your brain will play tricks on you in the first week saying \"this isn&apos;t working.\"</h3><h3>That&apos;s normal. Your brain is used to getting nicotine hits. It takes time to accept that the ritual satisfaction alone is enough.</h3><h3></h3><h3>After 30 days of consistent use, if you&apos;re genuinely not satisfied with your progress, you have 7 days to request a full refund. No questions asked.</h3><h3></h3><h3>We require the 30 days because that&apos;s how long it takes to break the mental patterns.</h3><h3></h3><h3>People who quit after 3 days miss the breakthrough that happens in week 2-3.</h3><h3></h3><h3>The guarantee protects you, but the 30-day commitment protects your success. Most people who fail quit too early, right before it would have worked. <strong>Give yourself the full month. Your future self will thank you.</strong></h3>"
    },
