    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text_8bxIgFiEY1sorYuq",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<h3>It&apos;s too simple, how can this solve my addiction?</h3>"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text_CpDD51kYrSBOclk7",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<h3>Your brain thinks big problems need complicated solutions. That&apos;s why you&apos;ve tried patches, gum, apps, hypnosis, none worked.</h3><h3></h3><h3>Here&apos;s the truth: Your addiction is 30% chemical, 70% ritual. Nicotine leaves your body in 72 hours. </h3><h3></h3><h3>The hand-to-mouth motion? You&apos;ve done it 100,000+ times. Complex solutions fight chemistry with more chemistry. </h3><h3></h3><h3>Lio replaces the ritual your brain actually craves. Ahmed tried everything complicated. They all failed. Lio worked because when cravings hit, he just picked it up. Same motion, zero poison.</h3><h3></h3><h3><strong>The addiction industry profits from complexity.</strong> They need you believing it&apos;s impossibly hard so you keep buying their products.</h3><h3></h3><h3>The hardest part isn&apos;t finding the solution. It&apos;s accepting the solution can be this straightforward. <strong>Simple doesn&apos;t mean easy. Simple means it actually works.</strong></h3>"
    },
